## Optical Physics vs. Algorithmic Blur

Modern smartphones simulate shallow depth of field through depth-map segmentation and bilateral blurs. However, real optical glass does something algorithms struggle to reproduce: chromatic aberration at the transition boundary, gradual bokeh petal distortion, and organic halation around specular highlights.

## The Tactility of Silver Halide

Film grain is not noise; it is structural. Unlike pixel sensor noise which is uniformly Cartesian and digital, silver halide crystals are irregularly distributed in three-dimensional emulsion layers.

> "A sharp portrait is not one with the highest spatial resolution, but one where the plane of focus isolates truth from surrounding distraction."

### Designing for Cinematic Restraint

When translating cinematic framing to the web, restraint is essential. As shown in our reference frames, deep contrast and deliberate letterforms create immersion without neon saturation or frantic animations.
